  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through Tuesday)\nIssued at 1218 AM MDT Wed Sep 2 2026\n\nThe uptrend in PWATs will continue Thursday night into Friday,\nwith values set to rise well above the 90th percentile and\nchallenge daily records through the weekend and into the middle of\nnext week as remnant tropical moisture gets into the mix. \nMoisture availability won't be a problem, but the upper high is \nforecast to move back west into the region and extend a stubborn \nridge axis southwest across NM. The upper high will cause above \naverage temperatures to persist across much of eastern and central\nNM into next week, with a moderate heat risk. However, ridging in\nthe mid levels of the atmosphere and anticipated cloud cover will\nlimit convective potential through at least early next week. The\nlatest medium range model solutions are showing significant spread\nwith regard to the amplification and placement of synoptic\nfeatures from mid through late next week, leading to a lower\nconfidence forecast beyond Tuesday. That said, given the abundant\navailability of tropical moisture and the upper high forecast to \nretreat back to the east, there is some potential for a wet period\nto unfold by late next week.",
